endobj
158 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (Answer: The block is split into two physical regions. FEOL \(front-end-of-line\) is the silicon-level device formation: wells, isolation, transistor gates, source/drain regions, and the contacts that reach up to the first metal. All standard cells \(the sensor-hub logic and the 512 flip-flops\) and the transistors inside the memory macros belong to FEOL. BEOL \(back-end-of-line\) is everything above the contacts: the alternating stack of wiring \(metal\) layers and via layers that interconnect the devices. The FEOL/BEOL boundary is therefore the contact layer between poly/diffusion and Metal-1.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
