/P 93 0 R
/E (Answer: The PDN is a three-level structure: \(i\) power pads \(VDD/VSS pairs on all four sides\) that bring current into the chip; \(ii\) a core ring on the top metals M6/M7 around the core and a ring around each macro; and \(iii\) a mesh grid of M5 \(horizontal\) and M6 \(vertical\) straps connected through via arrays to the M1 standard-cell rails. Multiple parallel paths from pad to cell keep the resistance low.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
