523 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 101 0 R
/E (Defence of the choice: the design is not the smallest possible die \(1.425 mm\) nor the lowest-power clock \(Option B\), but the best balanced solution. The 1.45 mm die keeps utilization at 71.3% with room for routing and decap; Option A gives low skew at a clock power of 12.6% of the block budget; the balanced routing strategy removes the 12-track overflow; and the sign-off checklist gives measurable closure criteria. Using less silicon, less power and fewer re-spins and iterations also lowers the energy and material footprint and the implementation risk, which makes this design the most defensible.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
